  @contract  only a MIDI take in a slot is a stop; holds at the ends, crosses to no other track  @ 475
  @contract  nil with no current instance  @ 476
  @invariant  a stop in another slot rebinds the tracker, and the rebuild resets the caret  @ 477
  @contract  resolves same-onset plan collisions in a per-column plan list (mutates in place)  @ 553
  @invariant  fromLogical is monotone but not isotone; two logical onsets can round onto one raw ppq  @ 554
  @contract  later-source-ppq plan (curr by tie-break) shifts up 1 ppq, else predecessor shifts back  @ 555
  @invariant  tail overlaps NOT resolved here; tm's universal tail pass owns every raw note-off  @ 556
  @contract  skips non-note plans/cols; optional `deleted` event-set excluded from the walk  @ 557
  @invariant  deleted corpses still live in col.events snapshot until next rebuild  @ 558
  @invariant  a freshly placed note is unbounded: endppq = util.OPEN, no authored ceiling  @ 1004
  @invariant  universal tail pass derives the real tail (next onset/take length) each rebuild  @ 1005
  @contract  caller pre-pins (ppq, ppqL, rpb) onto `update` before calling  @ 1006
  @contract  col nil only for a chord sprout (no column yet): no prev-vel to inherit, lane pre-set  @ 1007
  @invariant  notes ordered by entry; members re-resolved via cells[row], never held event refs  @ 1354
  @contract  arms on a note col's first pitch stop; pins (row, chan) until shift release  @ 1374
  @contract  returns true iff consumed; false lets the drain fall through (to value-digit entry)  @ 1375
  @contract  re-striking a gesture pitch toggles it off; freed slots are reused lowest-first  @ 1376
  @contract  spreadChan strikes walk channels up from home; plain strikes stack home-channel lanes  @ 1377
  @invariant  pins (col,row,part); overwrites a place keep-below, steps the sub-caret right  @ 1497
  @invariant  field re-read via cells[row] each keystroke; undo snapshots drive backspace-restore  @ 1498
  @contract  target, facility and key are remembered at take tier; the rest is per invocation  @ 2397
  @contract  with no target the whole of it is the notation snap  @ 2398
  @contract  the facility reads the target as points of the pitch line or as moves between strands  @ 2399
  @contract  purity is the moves facility's alone: how nearly a spelled interval sounds pure  @ 2400
  @contract  ambient is the moves facility's alone: the share of its sonority a strand rests on  @ 2401
  @contract  returns the steps whose empty shortlists refused the solve, else nil  @ 2402
  @contract  widen stretches those windows to the nearest points instead, so none refuses  @ 2403
  @contract  selection must be exactly one grid column; multi-col selection is a no-op  @ 3201
  @invariant  a 1-col block stays contiguous when it lands on the destination col  @ 3202
  @contract  cursor follows to the destination column (single event and selection alike)  @ 3203
  @contract  refuse if dest col has any onset in source's row extent (note: note-on; else any event)  @ 3204
  @invariant  source's row extent = selection's [r1,r2] for a block, moved event's onset row for a single  @ 3205
  @invariant  tails (either direction) clipped by tm's tail pass; never block  @ 3206
  @contract  per-frame overlay for the chain the caret addresses: notes to ghost, cells to suppress  @ 3781
  @contract  the gate is fxHostAtCursor -- a cell that runs no chain of its own answers nil  @ 3782
  @contract  the window is the viewport's rows, resolved on the producer's own channel  @ 3783
  @contract  notes[colIndex][row] = tm's record by reference; note columns only; first onset wins  @ 3817
  @contract  values[colIndex][row] = { val }; the producer's claimed targets only  @ 3818
  @contract  hidden[cell] = true for every plain original this chain parked; a host cell never hides  @ 3819
  @invariant  a ghosted row may also carry a real cell; precedence is the draw arm's  @ 3820
  @invariant  the overlay lands in the columns that exist; a claim materialises none of its own  @ 3821
  @contract  reentrancy-guarded; bails on no-take (page shows placeholder)  @ 4341
  @contract  takeChanged=true resets ec and re-reads resolution/length/timeSigs  @ 4342
  @contract  grid + ctx rebuild each call; pushMute at end  @ 4343
  @contract  a column's cells/ghosts carry while its events table + projection epoch are unchanged  @ 4344
  @contract  tv consumes configChanged only for transient-frame release and mute pulse  @ 4674
  @contract  rebuild is driven by tm's 'rebuild' signal — closes the (cm, tm) double-fire race  @ 4675
  @contract  non-transient FRAME_KEYS write while transient override active routes into releaseTransientFrame  @ 4676
  @invariant  releaseTransientFrame's cm:assign fires configChanged → tm:rebuild → tv:rebuild  @ 4677

